WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.356 --> 00:00:02.490
(dramatic violin music)

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:04.393
- [Queen Elizabeth] What's
your view of the Jubilee?

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:07.163
- You must do it.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:10.020
- Must I do that alone?

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.423
- There is only one queen.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:15.700
- Want to know more
about the Silver Jubilee

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.580
that revived the queen's popularity

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.700
and swept the gloom away from Britain?

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.110
Then keep watching for
the fascinating true story

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:24.250
behind the controversial event.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.117
I'm Laura Jackson and this
is "Beneath the Crown."

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:32.760
1977: the year that marked 25 years

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.840
since Queen Elizabeth the
Second's accession to the throne,

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.170
but much of the United
Kingdom wasn't in the mood

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.644
to get the Silver Jubilee party started.

00:00:40.644 --> 00:00:42.332
- What a mess, I mean honestly,

00:00:42.332 --> 00:00:43.165
can you remember a time

00:00:43.165 --> 00:00:44.403
when the country was in a worse shape?

00:00:44.403 --> 00:00:46.300
- Britain was struggling economically,

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.980
politically, and socially.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.430
There was mass unemployment, rising crime,

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:53.250
growing racial tensions,
strike after strike.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:54.997
- Right now the United
Kingdom is the equivalent

00:00:54.997 --> 00:00:58.100
of a patient dying on the operating table,

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.010
and the surgeons, no, the butchers,

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:03.500
no, sorry, the murderers
responsible for causing that death

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:04.690
are seeking re-election.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:07.730
- Despite significant
opposition due to the high cost,

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.160
it was decided the Silver
Jubilee celebrations

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.130
would go ahead on June the 7th.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:13.290
The actual anniversary

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.490
of the Queen's accession was in February,

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:17.840
a date which would also mark 25 years

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.720
since her father's untimely death.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.830
The Queen chose to push
the date back to June.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:26.280
Enthusiasm for Jubilee
Day was initially low,

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:28.760
but as it drew nearer, the
public warmed to the idea

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:30.710
as if it were an escape from the gloom.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.700
Suddenly, Silver Jubilee memorabilia

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.773
started popping up everywhere.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:40.400
Lord Snowden was tasked with
designing several souvenirs.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.990
- The powers that be
thought it might be nice

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:45.000
if someone from inside
the firm were to design

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.745
some of the memorabilia.

00:01:46.745 --> 00:01:48.360
- Oh Tony, you are clever.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.070
- Always happy to help my family.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:53.250
- Other items on offer was
somewhat less conventional.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:55.350
You could call someone on a Jubilee phone,

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:58.273
play someone with Jubilee cards,

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.360
strike a light with Jubilee matches

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:04.440
and even keep your trousers
up with a Jubilee belt.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.210
There was also a range of
Silver Jubilee underwear.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:08.870
The less said about them, the better.

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:11.170
One thousand pounds was
given to every borough

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:13.400
in Britain towards the celebrations.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.620
Street parties were organized
up and down the nation.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:19.210
Decorations sprung up everywhere.

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:20.710
There was a mood of jubilation

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:23.793
and togetherness that harked
back to the coronation.

00:02:23.793 --> 00:02:26.793
(upbeat jazz music)

00:02:27.716 --> 00:02:28.773
- How lovely.

00:02:28.773 --> 00:02:31.420
- Anarchic punk group the Sex Pistols

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:34.000
launched a blistering
attack on the monarchy

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.850
with their song, "God Save The Queen".

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:38.030
It struck a chord with many

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:41.970
despite widely banned
from British TV and radio.

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:44.210
There were fears it would
top the UK singles chart

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:47.290
in Jubilee week and
cause huge embarrassment.

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:50.840
The crisis was averted when the
song only reached number two

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:53.917
behind unlikely royal
savior Rod Stewart's track,

00:02:53.917 --> 00:02:55.500
"I Don't Want To Talk About It".

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:58.300
Rumors persist that a
record business conspiracy

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.480
may have kept it off the top spot.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.960
The queen was said to be
furious about the song,

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:03.880
although it was reported

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:06.343
that Prince Charles
found it rather amusing.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:10.750
But when Jubilee day
arrived on June the 7th,

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.170
the nation turned to celebration.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.220
The opposition to the day was overshadowed

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:17.450
by the estimated 10 million people

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.547
who attended street parties.

00:03:19.547 --> 00:03:22.900
There were roughly a 125 thousand of them,

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.160
with five thousand in London alone.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:27.063
Not even the rain kept people away.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:31.330
A global audience of
half a billion watched

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:33.710
as Her Majesty took the golden state coach

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:36.290
from Buckingham Palace
to St. Paul's Cathedral,

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:38.830
with Prince Charles
following on horseback.

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:41.240
The roar of the one million strong crowd

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.240
meant the coachmen couldn't even hear

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.510
the sound of the horse's
hooves hitting the road.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:48.980
A carefully choreographed
walkabout through London

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:51.600
allowed spectators to
indulge in a bit of chit-chat

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.030
with the Queen and Prince Phillip,

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:55.860
before they headed to
lunch at the Guild Hall.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.160
There, she delivered a speech

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:58.860
in the presence of the Lord Mayor.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:03.757
- My Lord Mayor, when I was 21,

00:04:03.757 --> 00:04:07.793
I pledged my life to the
service of our people.

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:12.630
I do not regret nor
retract one word of it.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:15.530
- That night, the Sex Pistols
took to the River Thames

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.720
for a protest concert, which included

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:21.480
playing "Anarchy In The
UK" opposite Parliament.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:24.540
It wasn't long before they were arrested.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.310
Looking back at it, it's crazy

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:28.200
that the sight of a golden carriage,

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.730
the ultimate statement
of wealth and privilege,

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:34.430
gave so much joy to a public
largely short of money.

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:36.690
The Silver Jubilee provided
an excuse to people

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:40.173
to share something and come
together on a massive scale.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.153
- [Queen Elizabeth] That's
the thing about the monarchy.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.973
We paper over the cracks.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:52.980
And if what we do is loud, and
grand, and confident enough,

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:57.550
no one will notice that all
around us it's falling apart.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:59.310
- That's the point of us.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:02.549
- [Queen Elizabeth] Not us. You.

00:05:02.549 --> 00:05:05.882
(energetic cello music)

